text:
maria: Heads-up — after upgrading the Node SDK to v2.1 the sample-app logs in dev are showing duplicated/changed request IDs across retries. Repro steps ready. Anyone seen this?

ajay: Yep, saw something similar yesterday. Trace spans split because the request-id changes on retry; looks like auth middleware re-issues it. cc @sam

sam: Can you paste the minimal logs + the init order for OTEL/hooks? We moved some init code in the quickstart last sprint.

maria: Paste of logs and a tiny repro:
```
[2026-03-10T12:00:01.123Z] INFO http request method=POST path=/v1/infer headers={"x-req-id":"abc123"}
[2026-03-10T12:00:01.456Z] WARN retry attempt=1 x-req-id=abc123-1
[2026-03-10T12:00:01.789Z] INFO http request method=POST path=/v1/infer headers={"x-req-id":"abc123-1"}
```
Init snippet from sample-app:
```js
// sample-app quickstart
require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node').start();
const auth = require('./auth-mw')();
app.use(auth);
const logRedactor = require('./redact-hook')();
app.use(logRedactor);
// previously redactor was before auth, now it's after
```

leo: Looks like two separate issues: (1) retry wrapper generates a new ID when headers are missing or auth refresh happens; (2) redaction/OTEL hook ordering changed so the redactor no longer sees the original header on retry -> redaction can miss thing. That combination also fragments traces.

ajay: That ordering change was accidental when we consolidated init in the quickstart. For parity with Python we need redactor to run first and OTEL to pick up propagated context before auth mutates headers.

maria: Also FYI the onboarding doc mentions REDACT_AUTOINIT in the Python SDK section (to force early redactor init) but there is no mention for Node. People following Node quickstart won't know to set it. Onboarding friction here.

ajay: Proposed short-term: (A) patch Node SDK retry to preserve incoming x-req-id across attempts if present; (B) revert quickstart hook ordering so redaction runs before auth; (C) update onboarding docs to call out parity flags. Longer-term: add CI e2e that simulates a retry and asserts single req-id and redaction.

sam: I'll pick up (B) and the quickstart PR. I'll also add a tiny test that runs the sample-app with a mocked retry to assert header stability. @maria can you attach the repro script?

maria: Gist with repro: https://gist.github.com/redwood/repro-reqid-retry (link pasted). Steps: run sample-app, curl endpoint with failing auth to force retry, inspect logs.

leo: I'll create a JIRA for SDK parity+docs (RDW-1423) and assign. Also marking as P2 because of potential redaction gap.

devex-bot: deploybot: quickstart-preview build pushed: https://ci.internal/redwood/quickstart/2048 - smoke tests queued.

maria: Thanks — leaning on @sam + @leo. If we can get the sample-app fix and SDK patch in this week we can avoid confusing customers onboarding. :+1:

ajay: Agreed. I'll raise a short RFC about req-id semantics for retries so we have a consistent contract across SDKs.

sam: Working on PRs, will tag reviewers.
